# Synthetic ballot reconstruction of the real 2019 Nauruan parliamentary election, Anabar
# constituency (6 candidates, 2 seats, 553 voters, Dowdall/Nauru scoring). Real per-voter
# ballots are not published; what IS published (Wikipedia's "2019 Nauruan parliamentary
# election" article, sourced to the Electoral Commission of Nauru) is each candidate's vote
# count at each of the 6 preference ranks and their final Dowdall score:
#   Maverick Eoe:      157/128/76/71/56/65   -> 286.117 (elected)
#   Pyon Deiye:        150/107/95/64/68/69   -> 276.267 (elected)
#   Ludwig Scotty:     116/37/54/56/59/231   -> 216.800
#   Riddell Akua:      83/73/61/86/180/70    -> 209.000
#   Jeb Bop:           29/116/158/104/96/50  -> 193.200
#   Transom Duburiya:  18/92/109/172/94/68   -> 173.467
# Because Dowdall/Borda scoring is linear in exactly these (candidate, rank) marginal counts --
# a candidate's score never depends on who else was on the same ballot, only on which rank
# position they themselves occupied -- ANY ballot set reproducing this same marginal table
# produces IDENTICAL scores to the real election, regardless of the (unknown, secret) actual
# joint ballot data. The ballots below are exactly such a reconstruction: a set of full
# 6-candidate permutations, computed via a greedy bipartite-matching decomposition of the real
# marginal table (a valid decomposition is guaranteed to exist since every row and column of
# that table sums to the same total, 553), verified independently (in Python, before this file
# was generated) to reproduce all six official scores above exactly. See
# BordaNauru2019AnabarFixtureTest.
